-- title:
--   The free structure F_M(A) of a minion generated by a finite structure (Definition 4.1)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathscr M$ be a minion on $(A', B')$ and $\mathbf A$ a finite relational structure whose domain is $A = [n]$ (more generally, a set enumerated as $e(1), \dots, e(n)$). The **free structure of $\mathscr M$ generated by $\mathbf A$** is the structure $\mathbf F_{\mathscr M}(\mathbf A)$, similar to $\mathbf A$, whose universe is the set $\mathscr M^{(n)}$ of $n$-ary members of $\mathscr M$. For a relation $R^{\mathbf A} = \{r_1, \dots, r_m\} \subseteq A^k$, the relation $R^{\mathbf F_{\mathscr M}(\mathbf A)}$ is the set of $k$-tuples $(f_1, \dots, f_k)$ of elements of $\mathscr M^{(n)}$ for which some $m$-ary $g \in \mathscr M$ satisfies
--   $$
--   f_i(x_1, \dots, x_n) = g\big(x_{r_1(i)}, \dots, x_{r_m(i)}\big) \qquad (i = 1, \dots, k).
--   $$
--
--   The free structure is the most general target: homomorphisms out of it correspond to minion homomorphisms from $\mathscr M$ to polymorphism minions (Lemma 4.4). For $\mathbf A = \mathbf H_2$ it is the 3-uniform hypergraph on the binary members of $\mathscr M$ used in Theorem 6.2.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The domain of $\mathbf A$ is any type `A` with an enumeration `e : Fin n ≃ A`; the index $r_j(i)$ is `e.symm (r_j i)`. The enumeration $r_1, \dots, r_m$ of $R^{\mathbf A}$ is quantified existentially (some `r : Fin m ≃ R^𝔸`). Because $\mathscr M$ is closed under minors, and in particular under permuting variables, this gives the same relation as any fixed enumeration. When $R^{\mathbf A} = \emptyset$, $m = 0$ and the relation is empty, since a minion has no nullary members.
-- source:
--   L. Barto, J. Bulín, A. Krokhin, J. Opršal, Algebraic approach to promise constraint satisfaction, arXiv:1811.00970v3, p. 23, Definition 4.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PCSPBLPAff_Symmetric_Setting
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicPCSP_Colouring_Minion

namespace AlgebraicPCSP.Colouring

open PCSPBLPAff.Symmetric

/-- The free structure `F_M(𝔸)` of the minion `M` generated by the finite structure `𝔸`
(Definition 4.1, arXiv:1811.00970v3, p. 23). The paper takes the domain of `𝔸` to be
`[n] = {1, …, n}`; here the domain is any `A` with an enumeration `e : Fin n ≃ A`, the element
`a ∈ A` playing the role of the index `e⁻¹(a)`.

The universe is `M⁽ⁿ⁾`, the `n`-ary functions of `M`. For a symbol `R` of arity `k` with
`R^𝔸 = {r₁, …, r_m}`, a tuple `(f₁, …, f_k)` lies in `R^{F_M(𝔸)}` iff there is an `m`-ary
`g ∈ M` with `fᵢ(x₁, …, xₙ) = g(x_{r₁(i)}, …, x_{r_m(i)})` for each `i = 1, …, k`. The
enumeration `r : Fin m ≃ R^𝔸` is quantified existentially; since `M` is closed under minors,
the relation does not depend on which enumeration is used. -/
def FreeStruct {τ : Type} {ar : τ → ℕ} {A A' B' : Type} {n : ℕ} (M : Minion A' B')
    (𝔸 : RelStruct τ ar A) (e : Fin n ≃ A) : RelStruct τ ar {f // f ∈ M.mem n} where
  rel R := {fs | ∃ (m : ℕ) (r : Fin m ≃ 𝔸.rel R) (g : (Fin m → A') → B'), g ∈ M.mem m ∧
    ∀ i : Fin (ar R), (fs i).1 = fun x => g (fun j => x (e.symm ((r j).1 i)))}

end AlgebraicPCSP.Colouring


